Z||000012||spideyfoot||05-20-2001||10:25 AM||||The term ricer is for the knobs with the small holes meant to go on Foreign cars, not you or your car. I'm just saying that other folks make Knobs that will fit our cars like Hurst $59, Momo $35-$85, Fiero Store $40, And Rodney has a cool turned metal laser etched ball coming out for $120. And no the Taz mats are not ricey there is no "R" in Taz. I'm just saying that's a Chevy thing. And personally I like some of the peoples Ricer cars its their little 75 pound I'm a bada$$ attitude that gets on my nerve If you look those guys are never facing the road they are watching you looking at their ride. But I guess I'm a hypocrite because I ride a Honda cbr 600F4 crotch(rice)rocket. So no offense meant at all.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero12_copy_1.jpg">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by spideyfoot (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||1
